== 4. Pintz targets: K_{k+1} on H u {r}, r a lambda-position; expect rho_crit = 1/(2k) -> theta*M_k > 1
Pintz k=2                                    k= 2 |L|=1 rho_crit=1/4    cert=True parity-blocked=False need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> YES at theta=1 (M_k >= 1.3859)
    dual inequality y = {0: '1/2', 1: '1/2', 2: '1/2'} 
Pintz k=3                                    k= 3 |L|=1 rho_crit=1/6    cert=True parity-blocked=False need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> YES at theta=1 (M_k >= 1.6460)
    dual inequality y = {0: '1/3', 1: '1/3', 2: '1/3', 3: '1/3'} 
Pintz k=4                                    k= 4 |L|=1 rho_crit=1/8    cert=True parity-blocked=False need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> YES at theta=1 (M_k >= 1.8440)
    dual inequality y = {0: '1/4', 1: '1/4', 2: '1/4', 3: '1/4', 4: '1/4'} 
Pintz k=5                                    k= 5 |L|=1 rho_crit=1/10   cert=True parity-blocked=False need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> YES at theta=1/2 (M_k >= 2.0041)
    dual inequality y = {0: '1/5', 1: '1/5', 2: '1/5', 3: '1/5', 4: '1/5', 5: '1/5'} 
Pintz k=6                                    k= 6 |L|=1 rho_crit=1/12   cert=True parity-blocked=False need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> not decided by bounds at hand
    dual inequality y = {0: '1/6', 1: '1/6', 2: '1/6', 3: '1/6', 4: '1/6', 5: '1/6', 6: '1/6'} 
   symmetric t* of the same graph (treating r as a sieve position) for contrast:
