== 7. Chen-type: n prime and n+2 in P_2 (P_2 position not parity-capped: cap 1)
Chen (P_2 cap 1)                             k= 1 |L|=0 rho_crit=0      cert=True parity-blocked=False need theta*M_k > 0.0000 -> not decided by bounds at hand
    dual inequality y = {0: '1', 1: '1'} 
twin (cap 1/2)                               k= 1 |L|=0 rho_crit=1/2    cert=True parity-blocked=True  need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> impossible for theta<=1 (M_k upper bound 1.000)
    dual inequality y = {0: '1', 1: '1'} 
n+2 semiprime only (lambda=+1 needed)        k= 1 |L|=0 rho_crit=1/2    cert=True parity-blocked=True  need theta*M_k > 1.0000 -> impossible for theta<=1 (M_k upper bound 1.000)
    dual inequality y = {0: '1', 1: '1'} (same LP as twins: the class blocks both halves)
